        <rdfs:label>Complex Power</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Complex Power, under sinusoidal conditions, is the product of the phasor (U) representing the voltage between the terminals of a linear two-terminal element or two-terminal circuit and the complex conjugate of the phasor (I) representing the electric current in the element or circuit.</skos:definition>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


