        <brick:hasQUDTReference rdf:resource="https://brickschema.org/schema/Brick#Dynamic_Pressure"/>
        <rdfs:label>Velocity Pressure</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Dynamic Pressure (indicated with q, or Q, and sometimes called velocity pressure) is the quantity defined by: (q = 1/2 * ρ v^{2}), where (using SI units),  (q) is dynamic pressure in (pascals), (ρ) is fluid density in (kg/m^{3}) (for example, density of air) and (v ) is fluid velocity in (m/s).</skos:definition>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


