    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://brickschema.org/schema/Brick#Disconnect_Switch">
        <rdfs:label>Disconnect Switch</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Building power is most commonly provided by utility company through a master disconnect switch (sometimes called a service disconnect) in the main electrical room of a building. The Utility Company provided master disconnect switch often owns or restricts access to this switch. There can also be other cases where a disconnect is placed into an electrical system to allow service cut-off to a portion of the building.</skos:definition>
        <sh:rule>na99033713e994d3fac6c613af3f33cc0b625</sh:rule>
